ng a Dalek story and he's not  shackled with the Daleks  so basic plot overview and synopsis I'll  try and avoid spoilers because I know  not as many people listen to the audios  as watch the show so I can't count on  most of my audience already knowing this  thing so plot wise the way it goes is  Davros and this has kind of already been  established in the show by this point  because Davros actually dies at the very  end of his first appearance and then  keeps coming back and it gets  established and and sort of firmed up  here that his the life support functions  of his chair you know that he uses to  get around because he's severely  disfigured and disabled has it's got  really phenomenal life support system so  he's as long as he's in that chair he's  almost impossible to kill so he is his  body is stolen by this head of a global  or not global like galactic level  company and I don't think they actually  say a year this takes place in but it's  it's sort of your generic unspecified  future where human society because we  they are explicitly called out as humans  it's not an alien society human society  is run by a handful of corporations it's  it's effectively implied that there  isn't really government anymore and that  capitalism is such that you know the  corporations are just running everything  at this point and you got and you get  your usual sort of dystopia elements  associated with that as one would expect  with that kind of setup but the the head  of one of these corporations and his  wife they steal what they think is  Davros as ba  so they kind of get a bit of bonus when  he comes around and they're able to  revive him now they're interested in him  for different reasons the the company  owner sees him as a general asset  especially once he's awake because then  he's like I can use this man's mind  because he was a brilliant scientist and  I can develop new tactics new ways of  coming at things new products new ways  to increase efficiency all this 